#: ../../../tools/index.md:18
msgid "Choosing a Tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:20
msgid ""
"Use the **Compile-Only Tool** to inspect the kernel source `lower()` "
"generates for an example file, on any machine and without launching "
"anything. It is the entry point behind the Compiler Explorer integration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:23
msgid ""
"Use **Analyzer** before benchmarking when you need a rough roofline-style "
"estimate from a `PrimFunc` or `IRModule`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:25
msgid ""
"Use **Layout Visualization** to inspect how logical indices map to threads "
"and local indices."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:27
msgid ""
"Use **AutoDD** after obtaining a stable failure signature and before filing "
"a large reproducer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:29
msgid ""
"Use **IR Lower Trace** to observe every pass and the final codegen step of a "
"full lowering pipeline. It supersedes **Pass Diff** and is the tool that "
"receives future improvements."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:32
msgid ""
"Use **Pass Diff** only when you need the legacy `TILELANG_PASS_DIFF` "
"workflow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:33
msgid ""
"Use **IKET** for CUDA timeline instrumentation when the external IKET "
"runtime is available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../tools/index.md:36
msgid ""
"Kernel-level debugging primitives such as `T.print` remain part of the "
"TileLang language. See {doc}`../tutorials/debug_tools_for_tilelang` for an "
"end-to-end debugging workflow that combines language primitives with these "
"tools."
msgstr ""
